paragraph.math:
$$\begin{array}{lll}
      {\det A} & = & {a_{11}\det A_{11} - a_{21}\det A_{21} + a_{31}\det A_{31}} \\
       & = & {2\det\left\lbrack \begin{array}{rr}
      0 & {- 1} \\
      2 & 1
      \end{array} \right\rbrack - 4\det\left\lbrack \begin{array}{rr}
      3 & 1 \\
      2 & 1
      \end{array} \right\rbrack + 0\det\left\lbrack \begin{array}{rr}
      3 & 1 \\
      0 & {- 1}
      \end{array} \right\rbrack} \\
       & = & {2\left( 0 - ( - 2) \right) - 4(3 - 2) + 0( - 3 - 0) = 0}
      \end{array}$$

example.paragraph:
Let $A = \left\lbrack \begin{array}{rr}
      .95 & {\text{.}03} \\
      .05 & {\text{.}97}
      \end{array} \right\rbrack$. Analyze the long-term behavior (as $k$ increases) of the dynamical system defined by $\textbf{x}_{k + 1} = A\textbf{x}_{k}(k = 0,1,2,\ldots)$, with $\textbf{x}_{0} = \left\lbrack \begin{array}{r}
      .6 \\
      .4
      \end{array} \right\rbrack$.

statement.paragraph:
It can be shown that the algebraic multiplicity of an eigenvalue $\text{λ}$ is always greater than or equal to the dimension of the eigenspace corresponding to $\text{λ}$. Find $h$ in the matrix $A$ below such that the eigenspace for $\text{λ} = 5$ is two-dimensional:$$A~ = ~\begin{bmatrix}
      5 & {- 2} & {~~~6} & {- 1} \\
      0 & {~~~3} & {~~~h} & {~~~0} \\
      0 & {~~~0} & {~~~5} & {~~~4} \\
      0 & {~~~0} & {~~~0} & {~~~1}
      \end{bmatrix}$$
